  "finalText": "T-1041 is triaged: it's now **sev3**, due **2026-03-17T17:20:00Z**, and assigned to **E-301 Yuki Sato**. Its status changed from new to open. I re-checked the plan against the live data before making any changes, and it matched.\n\n- **Severity: sev3.** The escalation matrix rates a VPN problem with team-level impact as sev3. The ticket describes about nine people on the Berlin sales floor who can't connect. The requester is a senior person in Sales, but that doesn't change the severity, because severity comes only from the matrix.\n- **Deadline: 17:20Z.** The ticket had no deadline. The service desk clock reads 2026-03-17T09:20:00Z, the same time the ticket was created. The sev3 response target is 480 minutes, so the deadline is 09:20Z plus 8 hours. No earlier deadline had been promised to the requester, so nothing was moved earlier.\n- **Owner: E-301 Yuki Sato.** The network-primary rotation owns VPN tickets. Yuki Sato is on call for it at the deadline, with a shift running 08:00Z–20:00Z, and their user record confirms they're in that rotation.\n\nI didn't escalate, because sev3 has no escalation rotation. I didn't change any other ticket.",
